1. one-sided write into A's memory
  B posts RDMA WRITE id 1 (12 bytes, key 0x1100) -> success
  A memory[16..27] = "hello from B" (A posted nothing for this)
  B completion: id 1 RDMA WRITE success
  A completion queue: empty
2. one-sided read, but the region does not allow remote reads
  B posts RDMA READ  id 2 (12 bytes, key 0x1100) -> remote access error
  B completion: id 2 RDMA READ remote access error
3. write past the end of the registered region
  B posts RDMA WRITE id 3 (12 bytes, key 0x1100) -> remote access error
  B completion: id 3 RDMA WRITE remote access error
4. two-sided send: first without, then with a posted receive
  B posts SEND       id 4 (12 bytes, key 0x0) -> receiver not ready (no receive posted)
  B posts SEND       id 5 (12 bytes, key 0x0) -> success
  A memory[200..211] = "hello from B"
  B completion: id 4 SEND receiver not ready (no receive posted)
  B completion: id 5 SEND success
  A completion: id 5 RECEIVE success
